1
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Bite the Bullet is a action, western, adventure film directed by Richard Brooks.

2
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:42,000
At the beginning of the 20th century, a newspaper organizes an
endurance horse race : 700 miles to run in a few days.

3
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:30,000
9 adventurers are competing, among them a woman, Miss Jones, a Mexican, an Englishman, a
young cow-boy, an old one and two friends, Sam Clayton and Luke Matthews.

4
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:18,000
All those individualists will learn to respect each other.

5
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Sam Clayton, played by Gene Hackman.

6
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Miss Jones, played by Candice Bergen.

7
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Luke Matthews, played by James Coburn.

8
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
Mister, played by Ben Johnson.

9
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
Sir Harry Norfolk, played by Ian Bannen.

10
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
Carbo, played by Jan-Michael Vincent.

11
01:36:48,000 --> 01:36:54,000
Bite the Bullet is a 1975 American Western film written, produced, and directed by Richard Brooks and starring Gene Hackman, Candice
Bergen, and James Coburn, with Ian Bannen, Jan-Michael Vincent, Ben Johnson and Dabney Coleman in supporting roles.

12
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:42,000
Brooks called it "my love poem to America.

13
01:54:24,000 --> 01:54:30,000
I love those people and the beauty of our country."

14
02:03:12,000 --> 02:03:18,000
The film explores themes of horse race, horse, endurance, ex prostitute.
